@startuml storage_concurrency
' Style and layout settings
!theme plain
skinparam rectangle {
  shadowing false
  borderRadius 10
}
skinparam interface {
  shadowing false
}

' The IStorageBackend interface is clean and has no knowledge of locking.
interface "IStorageBackend" as IBackend {
  +write(key, data)
  +read(key)
  +exists(key)
  +delete(key)
}

class "HDF5Backend" implements IBackend {
  ' Concrete implementation of I/O operations.
}

' The decorator implements the same interface and adds the locking behavior.
class "ConcurrentStorageDecorator" implements IBackend {
  -backend: IStorageBackend
  -lock: internal_lock_object
  +write(key, data)
  +read(key)
  +exists(key)
  +delete(key)
}

note right of ConcurrentStorageDecorator
  **Double-Checked Locking for Reads:**
  1. Check if key exists (e.g., in L1 cache). If so, return.
  2. **Acquire lock.**
  3. Check again if key exists. If so, release lock and return.
  4. Read data from wrapped backend (e.g., from L2 cache).
  5. Write data to cache if needed (promote to L1).
  6. **Release lock.**
  7. Return data.
end note

ConcurrentStorageDecorator o-- "1" HDF5Backend : wraps

@enduml